WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.996
Here are the headline numbers.

00:00:02.076 --> 00:00:05.664
SKiNN runs about three hundred times faster than JAM,

00:00:05.744 --> 00:00:12.239
taking roughly fifty milliseconds per image on a
GPU compared to about fifteen seconds for JAM.

00:00:12.319 --> 00:00:17.291
Its error is under one percent within the innermost
two-arcsecond region,

00:00:17.371 --> 00:00:23.381
with a median absolute error around 0.47 percent
and a ninetieth percentile of about 1.1

00:00:23.461 --> 00:00:26.150
percent across five hundred test images.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:32.240
The network maps an eight-dimensional parameter
vector to a velocity image and has about

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.662
seven million trainable parameters.

00:00:34.742 --> 00:00:37.431
It was trained on five thousand samples,

00:00:37.511 --> 00:00:43.106
split four thousand for training and five hundred
each for validation and testing,

00:00:43.186 --> 00:00:46.220
over roughly one day on five Tesla P100 GPUs.
